# Compiled binaries and dev artifacts never belong in source — the runnable
# bridge is the one the collector setup installs at
# {setup-root}/solo-agency-local-collector/bin/collector-bridge-{os}-{arch}.
# A committed binary here misleads the agent (wrong OS/arch) and bloats history.
/bridge-go
/bridge-go.exe
/bridge-go_*
*.backup
*.go.bak
_backup/

# The Go source of the bridge is NOT open source and does not live in this repo.
# It moved to the private repository soloagency/solo-agency-bridge on 2026-09-06,
# and this repo's history was rewritten to remove it from all 379 commits.
#
# What stays here is only what a machine needs to RUN the bridge and what an agent
# needs to USE it: the capability catalog, the industry dictionary, and the setup
# script that downloads a checksum-verified binary from the dist branch.
#
# This rule is the lock on that door, and it is load-bearing. Every working copy
# still holds the full source on disk — that is how the bridge gets built — so
# without this line the next `git add -A` republishes all of it and undoes the
# rewrite. Nothing warns you: the files simply reappear in the commit.
*.go
go.mod
go.sum
